$\begin{aligned}\underset{\sim}{r}\left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right)&=4\sqrt{3}\,\underset{\sim}{i}+4\underset{\sim}{j}\\\underset{\sim}{r}(\pi)&=-8\underset{\sim}{i}\end{aligned}$

$\begin{aligned}\underset{\sim}{d}&=\underset{\sim}{r}(\pi)-\underset{\sim}{r}\left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right)\\&=(-8-4\sqrt{3})\underset{\sim}{i}-4\underset{\sim}{j}\end{aligned}$

The distance between the positions is the magnitude of this displacement.

$\begin{aligned}|\underset{\sim}{d}|&=\sqrt{(-8-4\sqrt{3})^{2}+(-4)^{2}}\\&=\sqrt{128+64\sqrt{3}}\\&=8\sqrt{2+\sqrt{3}}\end{aligned}$

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.3cm,y=0.3cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{motionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{displacementRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[->,black] (-9,0)--(9,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,-9)--(0,9);
\path (9,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,9) node[above] {$y$} (0,0) node[below right] {$O$};
\draw[black] (0,0) circle (8);
\draw[->,motionBlue,thick,domain=30:180,samples=60,variable=\a] plot ({8*cos(\a)},{8*sin(\a)});
\coordinate (A) at ({4*sqrt(3)},4);
\coordinate (B) at (-8,0);
\draw[->,displacementRed,thick] (A)--(B);
\fill[black] (A) circle (2pt);
\fill[black] (B) circle (2pt);
\path (A) node[above right] {$A(4\sqrt{3},4)$} (B) node[above left] {$B(-8,0)$};
\path (-1,2.4) node[above,text=displacementRed] {$\underset{\sim}{d}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The red arrow joins the two positions directly; the blue arc shows the path travelled.

$\begin{aligned}\underset{\sim}{r}(2)&=6\underset{\sim}{i}+8\underset{\sim}{j}\\\underset{\sim}{r}(5)&=15\underset{\sim}{i}-13\underset{\sim}{j}\\\underset{\sim}{d}&=\underset{\sim}{r}(5)-\underset{\sim}{r}(2)\\&=9\underset{\sim}{i}-21\underset{\sim}{j}\end{aligned}$

The displacement points right and down, so it lies in the fourth quadrant.

$\begin{aligned}\alpha&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{21}{9}\right)\\\theta&=360^{\circ}-\alpha\\&\approx293^{\circ}\end{aligned}$

Keep the full precision of $\alpha$ until the final rounding.

